  "finding": "After the coordinator cold-booted the emulator, Gboard showed its full docked keyboard instead of the floating toolbar, and its suggestion strip showed a clipboard paste-suggestion chip with the current host clipboard item (a shell command containing a local path) in 14 of 54 distinct F9 frames: the R02 search/clear and full-list frames and both R03 frames. The chip text is absent from all UI XML, logs, receipts, the checkpoint, the run stream and the run directory (text search of every non-PNG file found none of it). Each frame's raw screenshot receipt was byte-identical to its PNG and is redacted with it. capture-index.json, commands.jsonl and the receipts keep the executor's pre-redaction hashes; sha256After below is authoritative for the committed files.",
  "detection": "Coordinator visual inspection of all 54 distinct F9 frames via 5 contact sheets. The font-scale frames that show the keyboard show only its icon row (no chip); G07, R04 to R10 and final frames show no keyboard. All 64 raw *.stdout.bin screenshot receipts were byte-compared with the saved PNGs before redaction; all matched.",
  "originals": "NOT RETAINED. The coordinator's script moved each original to the git-ignored /_backup_ns07_redaction/f-device5/ folder before saving the redacted image, but every move failed (relative destination path not resolved) while the save and the receipt copy succeeded, so the redacted image replaced each original in place. No unredacted copy of these 14 frames or receipts exists; sha256Before records what was there.",
